1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,141
Chapter five. Goliath.

2
00:00:03,491 --> 00:00:10,591
Across the country, the largest radio corporation in America wanted television for itself. It was called RCA.

3
00:00:10,791 --> 00:00:24,187
Its boss, David Sarnoff, sent his top engineer, Vladimir Zworykin, to visit the lab. Farnsworth showed him everything. Zworykin reportedly remarked that he wished he had invented it himself.

4
00:00:24,387 --> 00:00:29,210
Later, RCA offered him $100,000 for his patents. He said no.

5
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:36,644
So RCA filed a patent lawsuit against him. They claimed the idea belonged to Zworykin, who had filed an earlier patent.

6
00:00:37,094 --> 00:00:42,452
Remember that piece of paper? His old teacher Tolman showed up with the drawing from that chalkboard.

7
00:00:42,652 --> 00:00:54,754
In 1934, the patent office ruled in Farnsworth's favor. And in 1939, RCA finally agreed to pay him a one-million-dollar license.

8
00:00:55,654 --> 00:01:00,030
A farm boy beat a corporate giant. With a chalkboard drawing.
